{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And if a meal-offering on the griddle.</b> That he said 'upon me is a griddle meal-offering'; and it is a utensil that was in the Sanctuary, in which this meal-offering is baked over the fire in oil, and the utensil is not deep but flat, and the preparations of the meal-offering inside it are hard, for because it is flat, the fire burns off the oil. And all of them require three gifts of oil — pouring, mixing, and giving oil in the utensil prior to their making (Menachot 74)." "<b>Fine flour mixed with oil.</b> This teaches that he mixed them while still fine flour (Menachot 74)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:42.969984800Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}